name: sim.createHeightfieldShape
description: Creates a heightfield shape
luaSynopsis: int objectHandle = sim.createHeightfieldShape(int options, float shadingAngle, int xPointCount, int yPointCount, float xSize, list heights)
pythonSynopsis: int objectHandle = sim.createHeightfieldShape(int options, float shadingAngle, int xPointCount, int yPointCount, float xSize, float[] heights)
inputs:
1. options: bit-coded options:
    - bit0 set (1): back faces are culled
    - bit1 set (2): overlay mesh is visible
    - bit2 set (4): a simple shape is generated instead of a heightfield
    - bit3 set (8): the heightfield is not respondable
2. shadingAngle: shading angle
3. xPointCount/yPointCount: number of rows and lines of the heightfield.
4. xSize: length of the x side of the heightfield
5. heights: array of xPointCount*yPointCount height values
outputs:
1. objectHandle: handle of the newly created shape
